# Headless Browser Automation & Dynamic Web Scraping

This skill enables Claude Code and Google Antigravity to launch, control, and extract state from real headless web browsers using Playwright and Puppeteer. While basic HTTP scrapers cannot execute JavaScript or handle dynamic Single Page Applications (SPAs), this skill allows the AI to render pages, click buttons, fill out forms, and snap full-page screenshots.

---

## 🌐 1. Headless Browser Execution with Playwright (Python)

```python
import asyncio
from playwright.async_api import async_playwright

async def inspect_web_page(url: str, output_screenshot: str = "/tmp/screenshot.png"):
    async with async_playwright() as p:
        browser = await p.chromium.launch(headless=True)
        context = await browser.new_context(
            viewport={"width": 1280, "height": 800},
            user_agent="Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/120.0.0.0 Safari/537.36"
        )
        page = await context.new_page()
        print(f"[BROWSER] Navigating to {url}...")
        await page.goto(url, wait_until="networkidle")

        # Capture dynamic content after client-side hydration
        content = await page.content()
        await page.screenshot(path=output_screenshot, full_page=True)
        print(f"[✓] Captured full-page screenshot to {output_screenshot}")

        await browser.close()
        return content

if __name__ == "__main__":
    asyncio.run(inspect_web_page("https://example.com"))
```

